WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
I was in a fireside chat recently, and the person who was interviewing me asked me a question

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:12.680
about the increased levels of burnout and decreased wellbeing that so many people have experienced.

3
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.960
And she said to me, how do we get to the light at the end of the tunnel?

4
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.120
How do we get to this light where we feel well and happy?

5
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.160
And I thought about this a little bit, and I wanted to share this reflection with you,

6
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:34.440
which is that when we are in the tunnel, we don't need to be racing for the light.

7
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:41.360
Part of being in the tunnel, this tunnel of exhaustion or depletion is also recognising

8
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:48.320
that the tunnel has sides, that we can lean against the side of the tunnel and take

9
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.840
a breath.

10
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.480
We can sit on the floor and we can cry.

11
00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:01.120
We can name our emotions in the tunnel, the disappointment or the loneliness, and we can

12
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:07.720
ask ourselves, what is the value, what is the need that is being sign-posted by that

13
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.360
emotional experience?

14
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:17.200
We can reach out for other people's hands in the tunnel, and we can just hold those

15
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.800
hands metaphorically, knowing that we are not alone.

16
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:29.520
I've come to realise that so much of well-being is not about grasping for the light.

17
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.520
So much of well-being is about learning how to see in the dark.
